# Euclidean Algorithm (How `gcd()` Works)

Suppose

```
gcd(48,18)
```

```
48 % 18 = 12

Now

gcd(18,12)
```

```
18 % 12 = 6

Now

gcd(12,6)
```

```
12 % 6 = 0

Answer = 6
```

The process repeats until the remainder becomes **0**. The last non-zero divisor is the GCD.

